        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9811dfc5-f690-5c2b-834b-57b3bf35b323",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leon Uris\n- Works: Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin, Exodus, Trinity\n- Places: Berlin, Germany, East Berlin, East Germany\n- Events: World War II, Berlin Airlift\n- Organizations/Groups: Western Allies, Soviet occupiers\n\nFacts:\n- Leon Uris was born on August 3, 1924, and he became an American author known for historical fiction.\n- Armageddon, also titled Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin, is a novel by Leon Uris about post-World War II Berlin and Germany.\n- Armageddon includes a vivid description of the Berlin Airlift and depicts interactions among people from five involved nations, including the three major Western Allies and the Soviet occupiers of East Berlin and East Germany.\n- Leon Uris published the bestselling book Exodus in 1958.\n- Leon Uris published the bestselling book Trinity in 1976.\n- Leon Uris died on June 21, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
